{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaDJMxCY3SH1cQJZabgL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the three files for candidate 2 (round 4, exploratory slot), and the check command prints `OK`. Novelty against the other models and full convergence were not checked; admission tests those.\n\n- **Name:** `edge_weighted_alternation_memory`\n- **Hypothesis:** People remember a sequence with primacy and recency effects: flips at the start and end are held more strongly than those in the middle. So how often a sequence seems to switch between heads and tails depends mostly on its edges. Each person compares that impression with their own ideal switching rate. On some trials they guess instead, at a lapse rate that is their own. A streak or rigid alternation at an edge therefore makes a sequence look much less random than the same pattern in the middle.\n- **Motivation:** This targets the critique's strongest gap. Among pairs matched on alternation rate, people pick the sequence without a streak at its start or end 0.608 of the time; the best model predicts 0.529 (p=0.03, q=0.12). It also fits the brief's request for a memory or attention process rather than another summary of the stimulus.\n- **Model:** Each switch between adjacent flips gets a weight that falls off with its distance from the nearer end of the sequence. One shared parameter, `edge_decay`, sets how fast; at 0 it reduces to the plain alternation rate. The personal ideal rate, shared sensitivity and personal lapse rate are set up the same way as in the current models.\n- **Check result:** On the short 100-draw, one-chain test fit, ELPD-LOO was −954.0, close to the best model's −952.4. That is only a rough signal from a short run. The check also warned that PSIS-LOO was unreliable: 7% of trials had Pareto k > 0.5, well above the 1% tolerance. If that holds in the full fit, the model can still be admitted but won't be eligible as the exported winner.\n\nTwo risks:\n- **Too much like the lapse models:** Keeping the personal lapse rate means this model is close to `personal_lapse_ideal_alternation` except for the edge weighting. If the fitted `edge_decay` is small, it could be rejected as a near-duplicate.\n- **Grafting in an exploratory slot:** Exploratory briefs forbid combining mechanisms. I treated the ideal switching rate and the lapse rule as the existing base the new mechanism sits on, but a reviewer could read it as grafting."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3209,"cache_read_input_tokens":60514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3209,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7a75c3f-e13e-4da8-a55a-d350e440fa56","uuid":"b00c961e-05c1-4a24-975b-9ed700efa879","timestamp":"2026-09-30T19:56:30.179Z","request_id":"req_011CfaDJMWQyZ388tcsStZt8"}
